>
>
> On Monday, May 25, 2015 at 8:51:16 AM UTC+3, la gleki wrote:
>>
>> It's bothering me more and more how the current HTML/CSS
>> home-brewed hacks make the front page literally unusable on mobile devices.
>> When I was owning LMW on the old server I always checked it on mobile
>> devices and on desktops with different skins.
>>
>> I'd like to restore the state of the front page compatible with mobile
>> devices since 12% of all sessions are done from mobile devices.
>>
>> All suggestions to the front page should be first checked in sandbox
>> pages.
>> For those who would like inspiration they can look at national
>> wikipedias. Wikipedias in different languages have front pages with various
>> mobile-friendly and widescreen-friendly templates. Even minor adaptations
>> of them can lead us to a better front page.
>>
>
> I suggest doing all drastic changes on test pages. When people involved
> can confirm that on their devices those test pages are displayed fine then
> they can be moved to production.
>

This is how it was today before I came, how it was after I fixed a few
things (still the logo is not aligned to the center - something to be
fixed) and how the News page looks like on mobile.
http://i.imgur.com/0Ee24sG.png

The floating language bar made scrolling and reading the page on Opera
Mobile almost impossible. Yes, it's much more advanced but ... not
cross-device friendly.

As for the News page it's not shrinked to the screen but the legacy of some
Wikipedia templates taken for it still make it readable.

